Siblings are placed at independent random directions from their family centre (the first
model, kept for comparison), at a radius that matches the ordered layout's mean squared
sibling distance. 'edge' and 'interior' below are sibling indices only; no sibling is an end.
Under the ordered layout siblings would lie along an axis inside each family, because parameterisations
of a transformation are ordered rather than scattered. The holdout conditions are:
  edge      an end of the sibling axis is removed, retained siblings lie on one side only
  interior  a middle sibling is removed, retained siblings lie on both sides
  family    a whole family is removed, no sibling of it remains

AUROC below 0.5 means the novelty score is reliably backwards.

